      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "TALENT SCOUT (5) is the top pick after holding his margin to two and a half lengths when ninth in a BM68 at Morphettville Parks, a run better than the finishing position reads given it came in Saturday company. His earlier second to Charka at this track in BM64 grade was sound, and his proven record around this distance gives him the right profile. OVER YONDER (2) has the sharper last-start result, winning a BM60 at this venue as favourite by just under two lengths, and the return of Caitlyn Munro keeps that form line solid. PICK 'N' MIX (3) had no clear running until near the 200m last time and is better suited at 1210m, where her record is strong enough to make her a genuine danger. TRADE GAME (4) comes off a CL1 win at this track and gets weight relief, though 1210m is new territory after doing his recent racing at 1000m. STRAWBERRY SWING (9) has to be included on what she's done recently.",
